<title>EGYPT: Yield rises on Egyptian 91-day T-bills.</title>
<headline>Yield rises on Egyptian 91-day T-bills.</headline>
<dateline>CAIRO 1996-10-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>The average yield on Egyptian 91-day treasury bills rose to 10.261 percent from 10.260 percent percent at the previous auction on September 26.</p>
<p>The Central Bank of Egypt announced the following details (values in pounds, previous auction in brackets):</p>
<p>Maturity date: Jan 2, 1997 (Dec 26, 1996)</p>
<p>Average yield: 10.261 percent (10.260)</p>
<p>Value of bids accepted: 635.575 million (602.05 million)</p>
<p>Value of bids: 652.575 million (622.050 million)</p>
<p>Range accepted: 10.099-10.289 percent (10.002-10.285)</p>
<p>Range of bids: 10.099-11.512 percent (10.002-10.500)</p>
<p>Number of bids accepted: 177 (163)</p>
<p>Number of bids: 180 (167)</p>
<p>$1 = 3.40 pounds</p>
<p>-- Cairo reporting unit +20 2 578 3290/1</p>
</text>
